<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Sabotørstien — Fjellstue, Hjerdalen and Sabotørstien to Våer parking [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From the Hjerdalen departure beside Rjukan Fjellstue, follow the gravel road and bridge, then the marked forest path through Fjøsbudalen and the resistance-hut grounds. Descend to FV37 and continue through Våer to the museum parking boundary. Museum and Vemork bridge visits need separate arrangements. Plan about 6.6 km and 3–5 hours, with approximate climbing figures. The route requires about 730 m of walking on an 80 km/h road and 170 m on a 50 km/h road; a continuous pavement, usable shoulder and protected crossings are not established. Follow current pedestrian rules and signs, and do not attempt unsafe traffic passages. Use dry, snow-free daylight, check all access and closures, and arrange transport before departure.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright; https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. Source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/map?bbox=8.40,59.852,8.51,59.88. Changes: 13 directed original-node intervals from complete captured walking ways, removing only duplicate literal shared junction nodes. The selected route retains all 321 original positions; canonical display uses the existing source-vertex simplifier. No snapping, synthetic connectors, private/operator track coordinates or elevations. Two-dimensional planning geometry, not navigation-grade or legal permission.

